From 9577af86fbe20c519bee63f6b0a2b2f2402a036d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:36:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/30] nexus_engine: shader preparation while no game runs;
 precache stage; skip

- nexus_engine_prepare_shaders(json): runs Lichii's shader precache
  builder (shader_warm) for a game outside a session: reads the game's
  own files with the user's keys, finds the shader programs in its shader
  archives, converts the compute programs and writes the title's precache
  file. Skipped when the file is current (WarmFilesStale) unless forced.
  Progress (stage, done, total) and the result are in the status JSON's
  "prepare" object; nexus_engine_prepare_cancel stops it. A session and a
  preparation never run at the same time.
- The boot precache (LoadCallbackStage::Warm) is reported as loadStage
  "precache" instead of "preparing".
- nexus_engine_skip_precache: the loading screen's "start now"
  (ShaderWarm::RequestSkipWarm).

Additive: the API version stays 2; NEXUS checks for the symbols.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
